window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":74,"nomSourate":"Al-Muddaththir","nomFr":"Celui qui se couvre","nomEn":"The Cloaked One","nomEs":"El Arropado","nomArabe":"المدثر","lieu":"La Mecque","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":4,"nbVersets":56,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"يَٰٓأَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ","tradPropre":"O, toi (Muhammad)! Le revêtu d'un manteau!","tradEn":"O you who covers himself [with a garment],","tradEs":"¡Oh, tú [Mujámmad] que te envuelves en un manto!","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Interpellation du Prophète ﷺ enveloppé dans son manteau.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith de Jābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Al-Bukhārī) :</strong> Le Prophète ﷺ raconta qu'à la fin de sa retraite à Hirā', en descendant de la montagne, il entendit une voix l'appeler. Regardant autour de lui sans rien voir, il leva les yeux au ciel et aperçut l'Ange Gabriel (Jibrīl) sous sa forme originelle. Saisi de frayeur, il rentra auprès de Khadījah en demandant qu'on le couvre d'un manteau et qu'on lui verse de l'eau froide ; Allāh fit alors descendre ce verset.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>When and Why Surah Al-Muddaththir Was Revealed (v.1–7 — Hadith of Jābir in Sahīh Al-Bukhārī #4922 & Muslim #161):</strong><br><br>📜 Revealed when the Prophet ﷺ returned home trembling and asked to be wrapped in his cloak (<em>Muddaththir</em>), commanding him: <em>'O you who covers himself! Arise and warn! And your Lord glorify! And your garments purify!'</em> Verses 11–26 were revealed regarding Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah, who privately admitted the Quran's unmatched sweetness yet publicly called it magic to please Quraysh.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Cuándo y por qué fue revelada la Sura Al-Muddaththir (v.1–7 — Hadiz de Yābir en Sahīh Al-Bukhārī n°4922):</strong><br><br>📜 Ordenó al Profeta ﷺ levantarse a advertir a la humanidad, engrandecer a su Señor y purificar sus vestiduras; las aleyas 11–26 descendieron sobre Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>متى ولماذا نزلت سورة المدثر بالإنذار العام (آية 1-7 — حديث جابر في البخاري 4922 ومسلم 161) :</strong><br><br>📜 نزلت آمرةً النبيَّ ﷺ بالقيام بالإنذار وتكبير الله وتطهير الثياب وهجر الأوثان، ونزلت الآيات (11-26) في الوليد بن المغيرة حين شهد في نفسه بحلاوة القرآن ثم زعم للناس أنه سحرٌ يؤثر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-73-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"قُمْ فَأَنذِرْ","tradPropre":"Lève-toi et avertis.","tradEn":"Arise and warn","tradEs":"Ponte de pie y advierte.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ordre de se lever avec détermination pour avertir l'humanité.</strong><br><br>La mission prophétique passe ici à l'avertissement public afin de prévenir les hommes qu'ils rendront des comptes devant le Tout-Puissant.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Divine Command to Arise and Warn Humanity (v.2–3).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadith of Jābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī #4922 & Muslim #161):</strong> After the initial revelation in the Cave of Hirā', when Angel Jibrīl appeared sitting on a throne between the sky and the earth, the Prophet ﷺ returned home trembling and asked Khadījah to wrap him up; Allāh then revealed these verses commanding him to transition from personal preparation to public proclamation and warning.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>El mandato divino de levantarse a advertir a la humanidad (v.2–3).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Yābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī n°4922 y Muslim n°161):</strong> Cuando el ángel Yibrīl se apareció en un trono entre el cielo y la tierra y el Profeta ﷺ regresó a su casa pidiendo que lo cubrieran con un manto, Allah reveló estas aleyas ordenándole iniciar la proclamación pública del Mensaje.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>الأمر الإلهي بالقيام بالإنذار العام (آية 2-3).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>حديث جابر بن عبد الله (البخاري 4922 ومسلم 161) :</strong> لما رأى النبي ﷺ الملك جبريل الذي جاءه بحراء جالسًا على كرسي بين السماء والأرض رجع إلى أهله فقال: «زمّلوني زمّلوني»، فأنزل الله هذه الآيات إيذانًا بانتقاله إلى مقام الرسالة والإنذار العام.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ","tradPropre":"Et de ton Seigneur, célèbre la grandeur.","tradEn":"And your Lord glorify","tradEs":"Proclama la grandeza de tu Señor,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Proclamer la grandeur suprême d'Allāh (Takbīr).</strong><br><br>Louer son Seigneur et célébrer Sa grandeur au-dessus de tout associé.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>And Your Lord Alone Glorify (Takbīr).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Qatādah:</strong> Commands the Prophet ﷺ to proclaim that his Lord is far greater than any false deity or idol worshipped by Quraysh, establishing the foundation of *Allāhu Akbar* in prayer and call.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Y a tu Señor engrandece en exclusividad (Takbīr).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās y Qatādah:</strong> Ordena proclamar que Allah es inmensamente superior a todo ídolo adorado por Quraysh.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ﴾ : تعظيم الله وحده وإفراده بالتكبير.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس وقتادة :</strong> عظّم ربك وحده فوق كل ما يعظّمه أهل الجاهلية من الأوثان، ومنها شُرع التكبير في الأذان والصلاة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ","tradPropre":"Et tes vêtements, purifie-les.","tradEn":"And your clothing purify","tradEs":"purifica tus vestimentas,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Injonction de purifier ses vêtements, son cœur et ses actes.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Synthèse des exégètes :</strong> Ibn ‘Abbās et Qatādah l'expliquent par la purification de l'âme et des œuvres ; Muhammad ibn Sīrīn et Ibn Zayd par le lavage physique des habits (contrairement aux polythéistes) ; et Sa‘īd ibn Jubayr par la pureté du cœur et de l'intention.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Purification of Garments, Heart, and Conduct.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās, Mujāhid & Ash-Shāfi‘ī:</strong> Combines both physical purity—keeping one's garments clean from filth for prayer—and spiritual purity, keeping one's character, actions, and soul free from sin and treachery.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La purificación de las vestiduras, el corazón y las obras.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās, Muyāhid y Ash-Shāfi‘ī:</strong> Reúne la pureza física de las vestiduras para la oración y la pureza moral del alma frente a toda falta.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ﴾ : طهارة الظاهر والباطن.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس ومجاهد والشافعي :</strong> تشمل تطهير الثياب من النجاسات للصلاة، وتطهير النفس والخلق والعمل من الإثم والغدر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ","tradPropre":"Et de tout péché, écarte-toi.","tradEn":"And uncleanliness avoid","tradEs":"apártate de la idolatría,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ordre de délaisser les idoles et toute désobéissance (Ar-Rujz), selon Ibn ‘Abbās et Ad-Dahhāk.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Forsaking All Forms of Idolatry and Sin (Ar-Rujz).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Mujāhid:</strong> *Ar-Rujz* refers to the idols of pre-Islamic Makkah (such as Isāf and Nā'ilah) and every form of polytheism and disobedience; persevering in abandoning them draws the believer closer to Allāh.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>El abandono total de los ídolos y del pecado (Ar-Ruyz).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> *Ar-Ruyz* designa a los ídolos de La Meca preislámica y toda desobediencia a Allah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ﴾ : هجر الأوثان والمعاصي والمداومة عليه.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس ومجاهد :</strong> الرجز هو الأصنام (مثل إساف ونائلة) وسائر المعاصي، فأمره الله بتركها والمداومة على هجرها.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"وَلَا تَمْنُن تَسْتَكْثِرُ","tradPropre":"Et ne donne pas dans le but de recevoir davantage.","tradEn":"And do not confer favor to acquire more","tradEs":"y no des esperando recibir más a cambio.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ne pas donner dans l'espoir de recevoir davantage des hommes (avis d'Ibn ‘Abbās retenu par Ibn Kathīr), ni attendre de salaire terrestre pour la mission (selon Ibn Zayd).</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Giving Purely for Allāh Without Seeking Worldly Return.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Al-Hasan Al-Basrī:</strong> Instructs the Messenger ﷺ never to give a gift in order to receive more in return, nor to consider his own deeds and sacrifices as a favor upon his Lord, but rather to act solely out of gratitude to Allāh.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Dar únicamente por Allah sin esperar compensación mundana.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās y Al-Hasan Al-Basrī:</strong> Enseña a no dar buscando recibir más en este mundo ni envanecerse por las propias obras ante Allah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَلَا تَمْنُن تَسْتَكْثِرُ﴾ : إخلاص العطاء والعمل لله وحده.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس والحسن البصري :</strong> لا تعطِ عطيةً تلتمس بها في الدنيا أكثر منها، ولا تستكثر عملك على ربك بل استشعر فضل الله عليك.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"وَلِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْ","tradPropre":"Et pour ton Seigneur, endure.","tradEn":"But for your Lord be patient.","tradEs":"Sé paciente [con las dificultades que enfrentarás al divulgar el Mensaje] de tu Señor.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Endurer avec patience pour la Face d'Allāh face aux épreuves de la mission.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Steadfast Patience for the Sake of Your Lord.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Mujāhid & Ibn Zayd:</strong> Commands the Prophet ﷺ to endure the hostility and persecution of his people purely seeking the Face of his Lord.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La paciencia firme por la causa de tu Señor.</strong><br><br>📜 Ordena soportar con constancia las ofensas de Quraysh buscando únicamente el Rostro de Allah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَلِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْ﴾ : الصبر الجميل لوجه الله.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير مجاهد وابن زيد :</strong> اصبر على أذى قومك وتكذيبهم محتسبًا ذلك لوجه ربك وحده.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا نُقِرَ فِي النَّاقُورِ","tradPropre":"Quand on sonnera du Clairon,","tradEn":"And when the trumpet is blown,","tradEs":"[Pero ten en cuenta que] cuando se sople la trompeta [y comience el Día del Juicio],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Le souffle dans le Clairon (An-Nāqūr) annonçant le Jour du Jugement,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Sounding of the Trumpet (An-Nāqūr, v.8–10).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadith of Ibn ‘Abbās & Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī (At-Tirmidhī #2431):</strong> *An-Nāqūr* is the Horn into which Angel Isrāfīl will blow to herald the Resurrection; the Prophet ﷺ said: <em>'How can I enjoy ease when the Angel of the Horn has placed the Horn to his lips and inclined his forehead, waiting for the command to blow?'</em>","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>El toque de la Trompeta del Juicio (An-Nāqūr, v.8–10).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Ibn ‘Abbās y Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī (At-Tirmidhī n°2431):</strong> *An-Nāqūr* es el Cuerno en el que soplará el ángel Isrāfīl para anunciar la Resurrección.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>النفخ في الناقور (الصور، آية 8-10).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>حديث ابن عباس وأبي سعيد الخدري (الترمذي 2431) :</strong> الناقور هو الصور الذي ينفخ فيه الملك إسرافيل عليه السلام للبعث؛ وقال النبي ﷺ: <strong>«كيف أنعم وقد التقم صاحب القرنِ القرنَ وحنى جبهته وأصغى سمعه ينتظر أن يؤمر أن ينفخ!»</strong>.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"فَذَٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٖ يَوْمٌ عَسِيرٌ","tradPropre":"alors, ce jour-là sera un jour difficile,","tradEn":"That Day will be a difficult day","tradEs":"ese será un día difícil.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>un Jour redoutable et éprouvant,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Terror of That Difficult Day.</strong><br><br>📜 Describes the Day of Judgment as a Day of intense distress and hardship for those who turned away from Allāh's guidance.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La gravedad de aquel Día difícil.</strong><br><br>📜 Describe el Día del Juicio como una jornada de intensa angustia para quienes rechazaron la guía divina.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>شدة ذلك اليوم العسير.</strong><br><br>📜 بيان هول يوم القيامة وشدة كربه على المعرضين عن هدى الله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"عَلَى الْكَٰفِرِينَ غَيْرُ يَسِيرٖ","tradPropre":"pas facile pour les mécréants.","tradEn":"For the disbelievers - not easy.","tradEs":"Nada fácil para los que hoy desmienten la verdad.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>dépourvu de toute facilité pour ceux qui ont rejeté la foi.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Devoid of Any Ease for the Disbelievers.</strong><br><br>📜 While Allāh lightens the standing of Judgment Day for the sincere believers (making it as brief as an obligatory prayer), it remains heavy and relentless for those who died in disbelief.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Desprovisto de toda facilidad para los incrédulos.</strong><br><br>📜 Mientras Allah alivia ese Día a los creyentes sinceros, será sumamente pesado para quienes murieron en la incredulidad.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿عَلَى الْكَافِرِينَ غَيْرُ يَسِيرٍ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 بينما يهوّنه الله على المؤمنين الصادقين حتى يكون عليهم كقدر صلاة مكتوبة، فإنه عسير شاق على الكافرين.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"ذَرْنِي وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيدٗا","tradPropre":"Laisse-Moi avec celui que J'ai créé seul,","tradEn":"Leave Me with the one I created alone","tradEs":"[Oh, Mujámmad] Deja que Yo me encargaré de aquel que he creado, y vino al mundo solo,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Avertissement visant Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah (des Banū Makhzūm) :</strong><br><br>Créé seul sans fortune ni enfants à sa naissance, comblé ensuite de richesses étendues (v.12) et de fils restant constamment auprès de lui à La Mecque sans avoir besoin de voyager pour commercer (v.13), il s'obstina pourtant à renier le Coran (v.16).","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>When and Why Verses 11–26 Were Revealed Regarding Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Account of Ibn ‘Abbās & ‘Ikrimah (Al-Hākim, Al-Bayhaqī & At-Tabarī):</strong> Allāh says: <em>'Leave Me alone with him whom I created alone'</em>—referring to **Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah** (dubbed 'the Unique' among Quraysh for his wealth and status), who emerged from his mother's womb without wealth or children and will return to Allāh's judgment alone.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Cuándo y por qué fueron reveladas las aleyas 11–26 sobre Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Relato de Ibn ‘Abbās e ‘Ikrimah (Al-Hākim y At-Tabarī):</strong> Descendieron respecto a **Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah**, quien nació solo sin bienes ni hijos y comparecerá solo ante el juicio de Allah tras haber respondido con soberbia a Sus favores.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>متى ولماذا نزلت الآيات (11-26) في الوليد بن المغيرة المخزومي.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>أثر ابن عباس وعكرمة (الحاكم والبيهقي والطبري) :</strong> نزلت في <strong>الوليد بن المغيرة</strong> (الذي كان يُسمى الوحيد في قومه لثروته ورياسته)؛ خرج من بطن أمه وحيدًا بلا مال ولا ولد وسيقف بين يدي الله وحيدًا بعد أن قابل نعم الله بالجحود.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْتُ لَهُ مَالٗا مَّمْدُودٗا","tradPropre":"et à qui J'ai donné des biens étendus,","tradEn":"And to whom I granted extensive wealth","tradEs":"a quien concedí abundantes riquezas","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>avant de lui octroyer une fortune étendue issue de son grand commerce,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Vast Wealth Bestowed in Makkah and At-Tā'if.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Mujāhid:</strong> Allāh granted Al-Walīd vast herds, trade caravans, and orchards stretching between Makkah and At-Tā'if that yielded continuous harvests year-round.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Las inmensas riquezas concedidas entre La Meca y At-Tā'if.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Allah le había concedido rebaños, caravanas y vergeles que daban fruto todo el año.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>المال الممدود بين مكة والطائف.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس ومجاهد :</strong> بسط الله له الأموال والإبل والجنات بين مكة والطائف لا تنقطع ثمارها شتاءً ولا صيفًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَبَنِينَ شُهُودٗا","tradPropre":"et des enfants qui lui tiennent toujours compagnie,","tradEn":"And children present [with him]","tradEs":"y numerosos hijos atentos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et de nombreux fils demeurant toujours à ses côtés à La Mecque sans avoir besoin de voyager,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Sons Always Present by His Side (Shuhūdā).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Mujāhid & Qatādah:</strong> He was given ten or more sons in Makkah who never had to travel for trade because his immense wealth sufficed them at home—three of whom later embraced Islam (**Khālid ibn Al-Walīd**, Al-Walīd, and Hishām).","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hijos siempre presentes a su lado en las asambleas (Shuhūdā).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Muyāhid:</strong> Tenía diez o más hijos en La Meca —tres de los cuales abrazaron más tarde el Islam: **Khālid ibn Al-Walīd**, Al-Walīd y Hishām—.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَبَنِينَ شُهُودًا﴾ : حضورًا معه بمكة.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير مجاهد وقتادة :</strong> كان له عشرة بنين أو أكثر حاضرون معه في المحافل بمكة لا يحتاجون للسفر لكثرة ماله، وقد أكرم الله ثلاثةً منهم بالإسلام بعد ذلك وهم: <strong>خالد بن الوليد</strong> والوليد وهشام رضي الله عنهم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَمَهَّدتُّ لَهُ تَمْهِيدٗا","tradPropre":"pour qui aussi J'ai aplani toutes difficultés","tradEn":"And spread [everything] before him, easing [his life].","tradEs":"Y le facilité medios con holgura,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>tout en lui aplanissant toutes les facilités matérielles de ce bas monde.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Every Worldly Comfort and Authority Made Smooth for Him.</strong><br><br>📜 Allāh granted him longevity, prestige, and leadership among his tribe, yet he met these favors with ingratitude.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Toda comodidad y prestigio mundano facilitados para él.</strong><br><br>📜 Allah le otorgó larga vida y liderazgo en su tribu, pero él correspondió con ingratitud.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿وَمَهَّدتُّ لَهُ تَمْهِيدًا﴾ : بسط الجاه والرياسة وطول العمر.</strong><br><br>📜 هيّأ الله له أسباب الرفاهية والمنزلة في قومه ليختبر شكره.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ أَنْ أَزِيدَ","tradPropre":"Cependant, il convoite [de Moi] que Je lui donne davantage.","tradEn":"Then he desires that I should add more.","tradEs":"pero aun así anhela más.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Malgré cela, il convoite avec arrogance davantage de faveurs sans croire,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>His Vain Greed for Even More Without Faith.</strong><br><br>📜 Despite his rejection of the Quran, he arrogantly claimed that if Paradise existed he would be given even more wealth and children there.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Su vana codicia de recibir aún más sin creer.</strong><br><br>📜 Pese a negar el Corán, pretendía con arrogancia que en el Más Allá se le daría aún más.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>طمعه الكاذب في الزيادة مع كفره.</strong><br><br>📜 مع جحوده بآيات الله كان يزعم أنه سيُعطى في الآخرة أكثر مما أُعطي في الدنيا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"كَلَّآ إِنَّهُ كَانَ لِأٓيَٰتِنَا عَنِيدٗا","tradPropre":"Pas du tout! Car il reniait nos versets (le Coran) avec entêtement.","tradEn":"No! Indeed, he has been toward Our verses obstinate.","tradEs":"¡No! Porque rechazó Mis signos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>car il s'obstine à renier le Coran et à combattre le Messager d'Allāh ﷺ.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>His Stubborn Defiance Against Allāh's Clear Signs (v.16–17).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Because he knowingly opposed the verses of the Quran after recognizing their truth, Allāh decreed that his wealth and sons would steadily decline until he faced the steep, exhausting ascent of punishment in the Hereafter (<em>Sa‘ūdā</em>).","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Su obstinada hostilidad frente a los signos claros de Allah (v.16–17).</strong><br><br>📜 Por oponerse a sabiendas a la Verdad, Allah decretó la pérdida progresiva de su fortuna y una penosa cuesta de castigo en el Más Allá (<em>Sa‘ūdā</em>).","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>عناده لآيات الله ووعيد الصَّعود (آية 16-17).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس :</strong> لما عاند القرآن بعد معرفته بحقيته لم يزل ماله وولده في نقصان حتى هلك، وتوعّده الله بـ«الصعود» وهو جبلٌ ومشقة كؤود من عذاب النار.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا","tradPropre":"Je vais le contraindre à gravir une pente.","tradEn":"I will cover him with arduous torment.","tradEs":"Haré que sus dificultades vayan en aumento.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Le supplice de la montagne « Sa‘ūd ».</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith d'Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī :</strong> Le Prophète ﷺ a indiqué que <em>Sa‘ūd</em> est une montagne de feu en Enfer que le damné sera forcé de gravir sans répit : dès qu'il y posera la main, elle fondra, puis reprendra sa forme lorsqu'il la relèvera.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The torment of Mount Sa‘ūd.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith of Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī:</strong> The Prophet ﷺ explained that <em>Sa‘ūd</em> is a fiery mountain in Hell which the disbeliever (Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah) will be forced to climb perpetually.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī:</strong><br><br><em>Sa‘ūd</em> es una montaña de fuego en el Infierno que Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah será forzado a escalar sin descanso.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا﴾</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>حديث أبي سعيد الخدري :</strong> «صعود» جبل من نار في جهنم يُكلّف الوليد بن المغيرة صعوده أبدًا، كلما وضع يده عليه ذابت فإذا رفعها عادت.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Il a réfléchi. Et il a décidé.","tradEn":"Indeed, he thought and deliberated.","tradEs":"Porque él pensó y decidió [a sabiendas, desmentir el Mensaje].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La délibération d'Al-Walīd contre le Coran.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Récit d'As-Suddī :</strong> Lorsque les Qurayshites se concertèrent pour qualifier le Prophète ﷺ de poète, de devin, de magicien ou de possédé (voir aussi Sourate 17:48), Al-Walīd réfléchit, fronça les sourcils d'un air grave (v.21-22), se détourna avec orgueil (v.23) et déclara que le Coran n'était qu'une magie apprise et une parole humaine (v.24-25).","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>How Al-Walīd Plotted Against the Quran After Admitting Its Sweetness (v.18–25).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Account of Ibn ‘Abbās (Al-Hākim #3872 & At-Tabarī):</strong> After listening to the Prophet ﷺ recite Surah Fussilat, Al-Walīd told Quraysh: <em>'By Allāh, I have heard from Muhammad words that are neither the speech of men nor of jinn! Indeed, it has a sweetness, and upon it is a splendor; its highest part is fruitful and its lowest part is gushing with abundance, and it triumphs and is never surpassed!'</em> Yet when Abū Jahl pressured him to denounce it before the pilgrims arrived, Al-Walīd sat pondering and plotting how to label it.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Cómo Al-Walīd maquinó contra el Corán tras reconocer en privado su dulzura (v.18–25).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Relato de Ibn ‘Abbās (Al-Hākim n°3872 y At-Tabarī):</strong> Tras escuchar al Profeta ﷺ recitar la Sura Fussilat, Al-Walīd confesó ante Quraysh: <em>«¡Por Allah, he oído de Muhammad palabras que no son de hombres ni de yinns; tienen una dulzura y un esplendor insuperables!»</em> Pero presionado por Abū Yahl, se sentó a maquinar una calumnia para alejar a los peregrinos.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>قصة تفكير الوليد بن المغيرة بعد اعترافه بحلاوة القرآن (آية 18-25).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>حديث ابن عباس (الحاكم 3872 والطبري) :</strong> لما سمع الوليدُ النبيَّ ﷺ يقرأ صدر سورة فصلت رقّ لها وقال لقريش: <em>«والله لقد سمعتُ من محمد كلامًا ما هو من كلام الإنس ولا من كلام الجن، وإن له لحلاوة، وإن عليه لطلاوة، وإن أعلاه لمثمر، وإن أسفله لمغدق، وإنه يعلو وما يُعلى!»</em>، فخشي أبو جهل أن يسلم قومه فحثّه على الطعن فيه قبل موسم الحج، فجلس يفكر ويقدّر ماذا يقول.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"فَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Qu'il périsse! Comme il a décidé!","tradEn":"So may he be destroyed [for] how he deliberated.","tradEs":"Fue maldecido por la decisión que tomó.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>malédiction divine contre cette décision funeste et calomnieuse,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Condemnation of His Deliberate Scheming Against the Truth.</strong><br><br>📜 Rebukes him for knowingly fabricating a false accusation against Allāh's Word merely to please his tribe and preserve his status.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Condena a su deliberada maquinación contra la Verdad.</strong><br><br>📜 Le reprueba haber inventado a sabiendas una acusación falsa contra la Palabra de Allah por orgullo tribal.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>ذمّ تدبيره الكاذب على كلام الله.</strong><br><br>📜 توبيخٌ له على تعمده اختلاق البهتان ضد الحق إرضاءً لقومه.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Encore une fois, qu'il périsse; comme il a décidé!","tradEn":"Then may he be destroyed [for] how he deliberated.","tradEs":"¡Sí!, fue maldecido por la decisión que tomó.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>répétition solennelle soulignant la gravité de son mensonge délibéré,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Repeated Woe Upon One Who Rejects Truth After Seeing It.</strong><br><br>📜 Emphasizes the gravity of turning away from divine guidance out of pride after one's own conscience has testified to its truth.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Reiterada condena a quien rechaza la Verdad tras haberla reconocido.</strong><br><br>📜 Subraya la gravedad de dar la espalda a la guía divina cuando la propia conciencia ha atestiguado su veracidad.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تأكيد الخيبة والهلاك لمن جحد الحق بعد استبانته.</strong><br><br>📜 تكرير الوعيد لشناعة جحوده بعد شهادة فطرته ولسانه بعظمة القرآن.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ نَظَرَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite, il a regardé.","tradEn":"Then he considered [again];","tradEs":"Luego meditó [cómo desacreditar la revelación],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>il observa son assemblée après avoir réfléchi,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Surveying the Claims of Soothsaying, Madness, and Poetry.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Account of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> When Quraysh suggested calling Muhammad ﷺ a kahin (soothsayer), a madman, or a poet, Al-Walīd rejected all three because he knew every meter of Arabic poetry and saw that the Quran transcended them all.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Su examen de las excusas de adivinación, locura y poesía.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Relato de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Al-Walīd descartó llamar al Profeta ﷺ adivino, loco o poeta porque conocía todos los metros de la poesía árabe y veía que el Corán no se parecía a ninguno.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>نظره في الأقاويل الباطلة (الكهانة والجنون والشعر).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>أثر ابن عباس :</strong> عرضت عليه قريش أن يقولوا كاهن أو مجنون أو شاعر فنفاها كلها لعلمه بأشعار العرب كلها ويقينه بأن القرآن فوق كلام البشر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ","tradPropre":"Et il s'est renfrogné et a durci son visage.","tradEn":"Then he frowned and scowled;","tradEs":"pero [al no poder encontrar ningún argumento] frunció el ceño y ofuscó el semblante.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>fronça les sourcils et durcit son visage devant la vérité,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Frowning and Scowling in Frustration.</strong><br><br>📜 Unable to find any genuine flaw in the Quran, his face darkened and contorted as he chose falsehood over truth.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Frunciendo el ceño y demudando el rostro por frustración.</strong><br><br>📜 Al no hallar defecto alguno en el Corán, contrajo el rostro con amargura al elegir la falsedad.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ﴾ : تقطيب الوجه وتجهّمه عند الحيرة.</strong><br><br>📜 قبض ما بين عينيه وكلح وجهه حين لم يجد في القرآن مطعنًا صادقًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite il a tourné le dos et s'est enflé d'orgueil","tradEn":"Then he turned back and was arrogant","tradEs":"Luego le dio la espalda [al Mensaje] y se comportó con soberbia,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>puis détourna le dos en s'enflant d'orgueil,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Turning His Back on Faith Out of Arrogance.</strong><br><br>📜 He turned away from embracing Islam out of haughtiness and fear of losing his standing among Quraysh.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Dando la espalda a la fe por soberbia.</strong><br><br>📜 Rechazó seguir la Verdad por temor a perder su rango entre Quraysh.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ﴾ : الإعراض عن الإيمان كبرًا.</strong><br><br>📜 ولّى ظهره للحق استكبارًا عن اتباع الرسول ﷺ.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"فَقَالَ إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحْرٞ يُؤْثَرُ","tradPropre":"Puis il a dit: «Ceci (le Coran) n'est que magie apprise","tradEn":"And said, \"This is not but magic imitated [from others].","tradEs":"diciendo: \"Esto solo es hechicería que impresiona.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>en prétendant que le Coran n'est qu'une magie transmise,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>His False Verdict: 'This Is Nothing But Magic Handed Down!'</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Account of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> To deter the pilgrims from listening to the Prophet ﷺ, Al-Walīd finally claimed that the Quran was 'transmitted magic' because its eloquence moved hearts so deeply that it separated a believer from the falsehood of his idolatrous relatives.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Su falso veredicto: «¡Esto no es sino magia transmitida!»</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Relato de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Finalmente dijo que era «magia aprendida» porque su elocuencia conmovía los corazones y separaba al creyente de la idolatría de sus parientes.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>افتراؤه : ﴿إِنْ هَٰذَا إِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُؤْثَرُ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>أثر ابن عباس :</strong> زعم أنه «سحر يرويه عن غيره» لأن حلاوة القرآن تفرّق بين المؤمن وبين باطل أهله وعشيرته.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"ce n'est là que la parole d'un humain».","tradEn":"This is not but the word of a human being.\"","tradEs":"Es la palabra de un mortal\".","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et une simple parole humaine !</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Denying Revelation: 'This Is Only the Word of a Mortal!'</strong><br><br>📜 Contradicting his own earlier admission that it was neither the speech of man nor jinn, he publicly called it human speech.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Negando la Revelación: «¡Esto no es más que la palabra de un mortal!»</strong><br><br>📜 Contradiciendo su propio testimonio inicial, declaró en público que era palabra humana.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>قوله : ﴿إِنْ هَٰذَا إِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 ناقض شهادته الأولى فزعم علانيةً أنه كلام البشر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"سَأُصْلِيهِ سَقَرَ","tradPropre":"Je vais le brûler dans le Feu intense (Saqar).","tradEn":"I will drive him into Saqar.","tradEs":"En consecuencia, lo llevaré al fuego del Infierno.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Condamnation au brasier intense de « Saqar »,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Warning of Saqar (The Scorching Fire of Hell, v.26–29).</strong><br><br>📜 Allāh warns those who knowingly slander His Book with *Saqar*, one of the levels of Hellfire that consumes thoroughly.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La advertencia de Saqar (el Fuego abrasador, v.26–29).</strong><br><br>📜 Allah advierte con *Saqar* a quien calumnia Su Libro a sabiendas.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>الوعيد بسقر (آية 26-29).</strong><br><br>📜 توعّد الله من طعن في كتابه عن علم وعناد بصلي «سقر» وهي من دركات جهنم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا سَقَرُ","tradPropre":"Et qui te dira ce qu'est Saqar?","tradEn":"And what can make you know what is Saqar?","tradEs":"¿Y qué te hará comprender lo que es el fuego del Infierno?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>interrogation soulignant l'horreur indescriptible de cette fournaise,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Unimaginable Severity of Saqar.</strong><br><br>📜 Magnifies the awe and dread of the punishment prepared for arrogant deniers.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La magnitud sobrecogedora de Saqar.</strong><br><br>📜 Destaca la severidad del castigo preparado para los soberbios.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تهويل شأن سقر وعظيم عذابها.</strong><br><br>📜 تعظيمٌ لرهبتها في القلوب.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"لَا تُبْقِي وَلَا تَذَرُ","tradPropre":"Il ne laisse rien et n'épargne rien;","tradEn":"It lets nothing remain and leaves nothing [unburned],","tradEs":"[Es un fuego que] no deja nada sin quemar ni cesa jamás.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui dévore et détruit tout sans rien épargner,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>It Leaves Nothing Unconsumed and Spares Nothing.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Mujāhid & Qatādah:</strong> It consumes flesh, bone, and sinew, and whenever they are restored, the punishment begins anew without respite.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>No deja nada sin consumir ni perdona nada.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Muyāhid y Qatādah:</strong> Consume todo por completo antes de renovarse el castigo.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿لَا تُبْقِي وَلَا تَذَرُ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير مجاهد وقتادة :</strong> تأكل اللحم والعظم والعصب ثم يُبدّلون خلقًا جديدًا فلا تفتر عنهم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"لَوَّاحَةٞ لِّلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"Il brûle la peau et la noircit.","tradEn":"Blackening the skins.","tradEs":"Abrasa la piel.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>calcinant et noircissant les peaux.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Scorching and Blackening the Skin (Lawwāhatun lil-Bashar).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Its intense heat darkens the skin from afar as a warning to humanity.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Abrasando y oscureciendo la piel (Lawwāhatun lil-Bashar).</strong><br><br>📜 Su intenso calor ennegrece la piel desde lejos.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿لَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس :</strong> تلفح الجلود وتغيّر ألوانها وتظهر لأبصار الخلائق من بعيد.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"عَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَ","tradPropre":"Ils sont dix neuf à y veiller.","tradEn":"Over it are nineteen [angels].","tradEs":"Hay diecinueve [ángeles] que lo custodian.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Les dix-neuf Anges gardiens de l'Enfer (Saqar).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Récit d'Ibn Abī Hātim :</strong> Lorsque des juifs interrogèrent un compagnon sur le nombre des gardiens de l'Enfer, Allāh révéla qu'ils sont dix-neuf Anges rudes et puissants (Sourate 66:6). Le verset 31 précise que ce nombre sert d'épreuve pour les négateurs, de preuve convaincante pour les Gens du Livre (Torah et Évangile) et de renforcement pour la foi des croyants.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Why Verse 30 Was Revealed: 'Over It Are Nineteen' & Abū Jahl's Mockery.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Account of Jābir & Ibn ‘Abbās (At-Tabarī & Ibn Kathīr):</strong> When Allāh revealed that nineteen mighty angelic keepers guard the gates of Hellfire, Abū Jahl mocked the number before Quraysh, saying: <em>'Are the companions of Muhammad only nineteen? Cannot every ten men among you overpower one of them?'</em>—whereupon Allāh revealed verse 31.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Causa de revelación de la aleya 30: «Sobre él hay diecinueve» y la burla de Abū Yahl.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Relato de Yābir e Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Al revelarse que diecinueve ángeles custodian el Infierno, Abū Yahl se burló diciendo a Quraysh si acaso cada diez de ellos no podrían vencer a uno solo; entonces Allah reveló la aleya 31.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>سبب نزول الآية 30 : ﴿عَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَ﴾ واستهزاء أبي جهل.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>أثر جابر وابن عباس (الطبري وابن كثير) :</strong> لما نزلت أن خزنة جهنم تسعة عشر من الملائكة العظام، قال أبو جهل مستهزئًا لقريش: «أيعجز كل عشرة منكم أن يبطشوا برجل منهم؟!» فأنزل الله الآية 31.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"وَمَا جَعَلْنَآ أَصْحَٰبَ النَّارِ إِلَّا مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ إِلَّا فِتْنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ الْكِتَٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا وَلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ الْكِتَٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ وَلِيَقُولَ الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَالْكَٰفِرُونَ مَاذَآ أَرَادَ اللَّهُ بِهَٰذَا مَثَلٗا كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللَّهُ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَهْدِي مَن يَشَآءُ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ وَمَا هِيَ إِلَّا ذِكْرَىٰ لِلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"Nous n'avons assigné comme gardiens du Feu que des Anges. Cependant, Nous n'en avons fixé le nombre que pour éprouver les mécréants, et aussi afin que ceux à qui le Livre a été apporté soient convaincus, et que croisse la foi de ceux qui croient, et que ceux à qui le Livre a été apporté et les croyants n'aient point de doute; et pour que ceux qui ont au cœur quelque maladie ainsi que les mécréants disent: «Qu'a donc voulu Allah par cette parabole?» C'est ainsi qu'Allah égare qui Il veut et guide qui Il veut. Nul ne connaît les armées de ton Seigneur, à part Lui. Et ce n'est là qu'un rappel pour les humains.","tradEn":"And We have not made the keepers of the Fire except angels. And We have not made their number except as a trial for those who disbelieve - that those who were given the Scripture will be convinced and those who have believed will increase in faith and those who were given the Scripture and the believers will not doubt and that those in whose hearts is hypocrisy and the disbelievers will say, \"What does Allah intend by this as an example?\" Thus does Allah leave astray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. And none knows the soldiers of your Lord except Him. And mention of the Fire is not but a reminder to humanity.","tradEs":"Decreté que los guardianes del Infierno fueran ángeles, y dispuse ese número para probar a los que rechazan la verdad, también para que la Gente del Libro se convenzan y crean, y para que los creyentes fortifiquen su fe y no les queden dudas a ellos ni a la Gente del Libro. También para que aquellos cuyos corazones están enfermos [de duda e hipocresía] y los que niegan la fe se pregunten: \"¿Qué es lo que quiere demostrar Dios con este ejemplo?\" Así es como Dios extravía a quien quiere [extraviarse] y guía a quien quiere [guiarse]. Solo Él conoce a todos los que sirven Su causa. Todo esto es motivo de reflexión para la humanidad.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La sagesse du nombre dix-neuf :</strong><br><br>Fixé pour éprouver les mécréants (lorsqu'ils prétendirent pouvoir les vaincre), convaincre les Gens du Livre de la véracité du Prophète ﷺ par la concordance avec leurs Écritures anciennes, et renforcer la foi des croyants. Et nul ne connaît les armées de ton Seigneur à part Lui.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Fourfold Wisdom Behind Appointing Angels and Naming Their Number.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Qatādah:</strong> Allāh explains why He made the keepers of Hell angels (whose strength none can resist) and specified their number (19): as a trial for the polytheists, so the People of the Book may gain certainty (finding the same number in their Scriptures), so the believers may increase in faith, and to expose those with hypocrisy in their hearts; *'And none knows the soldiers of your Lord except Him!'*","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Las cuatro sabidurías de mencionar el número diecinueve.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Allah dispuso que los guardianes del Infierno fueran ángeles de fuerza irresistible y mencionó su número como prueba para los incrédulos, certeza para la Gente del Libro, aumento de fe para los creyentes y desenmascaramiento de los hipócritas; *«¡Y nadie conoce los ejércitos de tu Señor sino Él!»*","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>الحِكَم الأربع في جعل خزنة النار ملائكة وذكر عددهم (19).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس وقتادة :</strong> بيّن الله أنه لم يجعل خزنة النار إلا ملائكة لا يطيق أحدٌ قوّتهم، وجعل عدتهم فتنةً للمشركين، ويقينًا لأهل الكتاب لموافقته ما في كتبهم، وزيادةً في إيمان المؤمنين، وفضيحةً للمنافقين؛ ﴿وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ﴾.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِ","tradPropre":"Non!... Par la lune!","tradEn":"No! By the moon","tradEs":"[No es como pretenden los que rechazan la revelación, lo] juro por la Luna,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style=\"color:#ffffff;\">Il n’arrivera pas, comme le prétend un certain polythéiste, que ses compagnons viendront à bout des gardiens de l’Enfer et qu’ils finiront par en sortir.</strong> Allah prête ici serment par la lune.","explicationEn":"32. The statement is not as claimed by some idolaters that he will suffice his companions against the wardens of Hell and take them out of it. Allah took an oath by the moon.","explicationEs":"32. La realidad no es como afirman los idólatras, de que junto a sus compañeros podrán derrotar a los guardianes del Infierno y salir de allí. Allah lo jura por la Luna.","explicationAr":"ليس القول كما يزعم بعض المشركين أنه يكفي أصحابه خَزَنة جهنم حتى يُجْهِضهم عنها، أقسم الله بالقمر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"وَالَّيْلِ إِذْ أَدْبَرَ","tradPropre":"Et par la nuit quand elle se retire!","tradEn":"And [by] the night when it departs","tradEs":"por la noche cuando desaparece,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis il prête serment par la nuit qui se termine","explicationEn":"33. He took an oath by the night when it departs.","explicationEs":"33. Allah hace un juramento por la noche cuando desaparece.","explicationAr":"وأقسم بالليل حين ولّى.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَالصُّبْحِ إِذَآ أَسْفَرَ","tradPropre":"Et par l'aurore quand elle se découvre!","tradEn":"And [by] the morning when it brightens,","tradEs":"por la mañana cuando resplandece,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"et par l’aube qui apparaît.","explicationEn":"34. He took an oath by the morning when it lights up.","explicationEs":"34. También jura por la mañana cuando se ilumina.","explicationAr":"وأقسم بالصبح إذا أضاء.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهَا لَإِحْدَى الْكُبَرِ","tradPropre":"[Saqar] est l'un des plus grands [malheurs]","tradEn":"Indeed, the Fire is of the greatest [afflictions]","tradEs":"que [el Infierno] es uno de los mayores [avisos],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Feu de l’Enfer est un des plus grands malheurs","explicationEn":"35. The fire of Hell is one the great calamities.","explicationEs":"35. Él jura que el fuego del Infierno es una de las grandes calamidades.","explicationAr":"إنّ نار جهنم لإحدى البلايا العظيمة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"نَذِيرٗا لِّلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"un avertissement, pour les humains.","tradEn":"As a warning to humanity -","tradEs":"una advertencia para los seres humanos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"et un avertissement qui menace et effraie les humains.","explicationEn":"36. In order to strike terror and fear in people.","explicationEs":"36. Para advertir a los seres humanos.","explicationAr":"ترهيبًا وتخويفًا للناس.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"لِمَن شَآءَ مِنكُمْ أَن يَتَقَدَّمَ أَوْ يَتَأَخَّرَ","tradPropre":"Pour qui d'entre vous, veut avancer ou reculer.","tradEn":"To whoever wills among you to proceed or stay behind.","tradEs":"Para que cada uno elija [libremente] obrar bien u obrar mal.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour qui d’entre vous, ô gens, désire avancer dans la foi et les bonnes œuvres ou bien reculer dans la mécréance et les péchés.","explicationEn":"37. Whoever from amongst you, O people, wishes to go forward with faith in Allah and righteous actions, or to lag behind by disbelief and sins.","explicationEs":"37. Para quien desee tener fe en Allah y realizar obras justas, o desee mantenerse en la incredulidad y cometer pecados.","explicationAr":"لمن شاء منكم - أيها الناس - أن يتقدم بالإيمان بالله والعمل الصالح، أو يتأخر بالكفر والمعاصي.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"كُلُّ نَفْسِ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ","tradPropre":"Toute âme est l'otage de ce qu'elle a acquis.","tradEn":"Every soul, for what it has earned, will be retained","tradEs":"Toda alma será rehén de lo que haya hecho,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Toute âme demeure responsable et otage de ses propres actes,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Individual Accountability: Every Soul Held in Pledge for Its Deeds (v.38–39).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> Every soul is held accountable and bound by what it has earned of deeds, except the Companions of the Right.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Responsabilidad individual: Toda alma es rehén de sus obras (v.38–39).</strong><br><br>📜 Toda persona responde por lo que ha obrado, salvo los Compañeros de la Derecha.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>مسؤولية كل نفس عن كسبها : ﴿كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ﴾ (آية 38-39).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس :</strong> كل نفس مرتهنة بعملها يوم القيامة إلا أصحاب اليمين.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"إِلَّآ أَصْحَٰبَ الْيَمِينِ","tradPropre":"Sauf les gens de la droite (les élus):","tradEn":"Except the companions of the right,","tradEs":"salvo los [bienaventurados] de la derecha.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>hormis les Gens de la Droite (les élus sauvés par leur foi),</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Deliverance of the Companions of the Right (Ashāb al-Yamīn).</strong><br><br>📜 Through Allāh's grace and their sincere faith and righteous deeds, the people of the Right are freed from captivity to sin and admitted into Gardens.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La salvación de los Compañeros de la Derecha (Ashāb al-Yamīn).</strong><br><br>📜 Por la gracia de Allah y su fe sincera, quedan liberados en los Jardines del Paraíso.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>نجاة أصحاب اليمين وفكاكهم بصالح أعمالهم.</strong><br><br>📜 فكّوا رقابهم بتوحيد الله وطاعته ففازوا بجنات النعيم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"فِي جَنَّٰتٖ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ","tradPropre":"dans des Jardins, ils s'interrogeront","tradEn":"[Who will be] in gardens, questioning each other","tradEs":"[Ellos estarán] en jardines y se preguntarán unos a otros","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, ils seront dans des Jardins où ils se questionneront les uns les autres","explicationEn":"40. On the Day of Judgement, they will be in gardens asking one another.","explicationEs":"40. En el Día del Juicio, estarán en jardines preguntándose unos a otros.","explicationAr":"وهم يوم القيامة في جنات يسأل بعضهم بعضًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"عَنِ الْمُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"au sujet des criminels:","tradEn":"About the criminals,","tradEs":"acerca de [la situación] de los criminales.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"au sujet des criminels qui se sont conduits eux-mêmes en péchant, à la perdition.","explicationEn":"41. About the disbelievers who destroyed themselves by the sins they committed.","explicationEs":"41. Sobre los incrédulos que se destruyeron a sí mismos con los pecados que cometieron.","explicationAr":"عن الكافرين الذين أهلكوا أنفسهم بما عملوا من المعاصي.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"مَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِي سَقَرَ","tradPropre":"«Qu'est-ce qui vous a acheminés à Saqar?»","tradEn":"[And asking them], \"What put you into Saqar?\"","tradEs":"Y les preguntarán: \"¿Qué fue lo que los llevó al fuego del Infierno?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui interrogeront les criminels depuis le Paradis sur ce qui les a conduits dans « Saqar » :</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The Dialogue Between Paradise and Hell: 'What Led You into Saqar?' (v.40–47).</strong><br><br>📜 From their lofty Gardens, the believers ask the criminals what brought them into Hellfire, receiving a four-part confession that summarizes the causes of ruin.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>El diálogo entre el Paraíso y el Infierno: «¿Qué os condujo a Saqar?» (v.40–47).</strong><br><br>📜 Los creyentes preguntan a los culpables qué los llevó al Fuego, recibiendo una confesión de cuatro causas.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>حوار أهل الجنة مع المجرمين : ﴿مَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِي سَقَرَ﴾ (آية 40-47).</strong><br><br>📜 يسأل المؤمنون في الجنات المجرمين عن الأسباب التي أوردتهم النار فيعترفون بأربع موبقات.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"قَالُواْ لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّينَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «Nous n'étions pas de ceux qui faisaient la Salât,","tradEn":"They will say, \"We were not of those who prayed,","tradEs":"Ellos responderán: \"Fue que no cumplíamos con la oración,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>les damnés avoueront qu'ils n'accomplissaient pas la prière obligatoire,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>First Cause of Ruin: 'We Were Not of Those Who Prayed!'</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn Mas‘ūd & Ash-Shāfi‘ī:</strong> They neglected the first duty toward the Creator: establishing prayer and worshipping Allāh alone.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Primera causa: «¡No nos contábamos entre los que rezaban!»</strong><br><br>📜 Abandonaron el primer deber hacia el Creador: la oración y el culto exclusivo a Allah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>السبب الأول : ﴿قَالُوا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّينَ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 ضيّعوا حق الخالق الأعظم بترك التوحيد والصلاة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"وَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِينَ","tradPropre":"et nous ne nourrissions pas le pauvre,","tradEn":"Nor did we used to feed the poor.","tradEs":"no dábamos de comer al pobre,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qu'ils refusaient de nourrir les pauvres et les nécessiteux,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Second Cause of Ruin: 'Nor Did We Feed the Poor!'</strong><br><br>📜 Along with abandoning Allāh's right (prayer), they abandoned the right of creation by withholding charity and compassion from the needy.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Segunda causa: «¡Ni alimentábamos al pobre!»</strong><br><br>📜 Junto con abandonar el derecho de Allah, negaron la compasión y la caridad hacia los necesitados.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>السبب الثاني : ﴿وَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِينَ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 جمعوا بين تضييع حق الله وتضييع حق الخلق بمنع الإحسان إلى الفقراء.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"وَكُنَّا نَخُوضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِينَ","tradPropre":"et nous nous associions à ceux qui tenaient des conversations futiles,","tradEn":"And we used to enter into vain discourse with those who engaged [in it],","tradEs":"nos entreteníamos difamando [la revelación] junto a quienes retuercen la lógica para negar la verdad,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qu'ils se mêlaient aux conversations vaines et moqueuses contre la Révélation,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Third Cause: Indulging in Vain Mockery Against the Truth.</strong><br><br>📜 They used to join those who engaged in falsehood and ridiculed the revelations of Allāh.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Tercera causa: Sumergirse en vanidades y burlas contra la Verdad.</strong><br><br>📜 Se unían a quienes hablaban con falsedad contra los signos de Allah.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>السبب الثالث : ﴿وَكُنَّا نَخُوضُ مَعَ الْخَائِضِينَ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 كانوا يشاركون أهل الباطل في الاستهزاء بآيات الله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"وَكُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّينِ","tradPropre":"et nous traitions de mensonge le jour de la Rétribution,","tradEn":"And we used to deny the Day of Recompense","tradEs":"y desmentíamos la existencia del Día del Juicio","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et qu'ils démentaient le Jour du Jugement,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Fourth Cause: Denying the Day of Recompense (Yawm ad-Dīn).</strong><br><br>📜 Because they denied the Resurrection and the Reckoning, they lived without moral restraint.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Cuarta causa: Desmentir el Día del Juicio (Yawm ad-Dīn).</strong><br><br>📜 Su negación de la Resurrección los llevó a vivir sin freno moral.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>السبب الرابع : ﴿وَكُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّينِ﴾.</strong><br><br>📜 إنكارهم للبعث والجزاء جرّأهم على المعاصي والظلم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰٓ أَتَىٰنَا الْيَقِينُ","tradPropre":"jusqu'à ce que nous vînt la vérité évidente [la mort]».","tradEn":"Until there came to us the certainty.\"","tradEs":"hasta que nos alcanzó la muerte [y con ella la certeza]\".","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>jusqu'à ce que la mort (l'évidence certaine) vienne les surprendre.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>'Until the Certainty (Death) Came to Us!'</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās & Qatādah (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī):</strong> *Al-Yaqīn* here means death, at which point what they used to deny became undeniable reality and the time for repentance expired.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>«¡Hasta que nos llegó la Certeza (la muerte)!»</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās y Qatādah (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī):</strong> *Al-Yaqīn* es la muerte, instante en que ven con certeza lo que antes negaban.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿حَتَّىٰ أَتَانَا الْيَقِينُ﴾ (الموت).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس وقتادة (صحيح البخاري) :</strong> اليقين هنا هو الموت الذي ينكشف عنده الغطاء وينقطع أوان التوبة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"فَمَا تَنفَعُهُمْ شَفَٰعَةُ الشَّٰفِعِينَ","tradPropre":"Ne leur profitera point donc, l'intercession des intercesseurs.","tradEn":"So there will not benefit them the intercession of [any] intercessors.","tradEs":"A estos no les beneficiará intercesión alguna.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, l’intercession des anges, des prophètes et des pieux ne leur profitera pas, car l’une des conditions de l’acceptation de l’intercession est que le bénéficiaire de cette intercession soit agréé.","explicationEn":"48. On the Day of Judgment, the mediation of intercessors from the angels, prophets and pious ones, will not benefit them, because the requirement for the acceptance of intercession is that the thing for which intercession is made must be approved.","explicationEs":"48. En el Día del Juicio, la mediación de los intercesores de entre los ángeles, los profetas y los piadosos, no los beneficiará, porque el requisito para la aceptación de la intercesión es que el propósito por el cual se hace la intercesión debe ser aprobado por Allah.","explicationAr":"فما تنفعهم يوم القيامة وساطة الشافعين من الملائكة والنبيين والصالحين؛ لأن من شرط قَبول الشفاعة الرضا عن المشفوع له.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"فَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِينَ","tradPropre":"Qu'ont-ils à se détourner du Rappel?","tradEn":"Then what is [the matter] with them that they are, from the reminder, turning away","tradEs":"¿Qué les pasa que se apartan de la amonestación [del Corán]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour quelle raison ces polythéistes se détournent-ils du Coran?","explicationEn":"49. What has made these idolaters turn away from the Qur’ān?!","explicationEs":"49. ¿Qué ha hecho que estos idólatras se alejen del Corán?","explicationAr":"أي شيء جعل هؤلاء المشركين معرضين عن القرآن؟!","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"كَأَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٞ مُّسْتَنفِرَةٞ","tradPropre":"Ils sont comme des onagres épouvantés,","tradEn":"As if they were alarmed donkeys","tradEs":"como si fueran cebras espantadas","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comparaison des négateurs fuyant le Rappel à des ânes sauvages effarouchés,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Why Do They Turn Away from the Reminder Like Startled Wild Donkeys? (v.49–51).</strong><br><br>📜 Likens the polytheists' blind flight from the Quran's guidance to wild zebras bolting in panic.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>¿Por qué huyen del Recordatorio como asnos salvajes espantados? (v.49–51).</strong><br><br>📜 Compara la huida ciega de los politeístas ante el Corán con cebras que escapan despavoridas.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تشبيه إعراض المشركين عن التذكرة بالحُمُر المستنفرة (آية 49-51).</strong><br><br>📜 تصوير نفورهم الأعمى عن سماع القرآن بالحمر الوحشية النافرة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"فَرَّتْ مِن قَسْوَرَةِ","tradPropre":"s'enfuyant devant un lion.","tradEn":"Fleeing from a lion?","tradEs":"huyendo de un león?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui s'enfuient à toute allure devant un lion (Qaswarah).</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Fleeing from a Lion (Al-Qaswarah).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> *Al-Qaswarah* means the lion (or archers hunting); instead of approaching the Quran that brings them life, they flee from it as if fleeing from death.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Huyendo de un león (Al-Qaswarah).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Ibn ‘Abbās:</strong> *Al-Qaswarah* significa el león (o los cazadores); en vez de acercarse al Corán que les da vida, huyen de él.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿فَرَّتْ مِن قَسْوَرَةٍ﴾ (الأسد أو الرماة).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير ابن عباس :</strong> القسورة هو الأسد (أو الرماة القناصون)؛ يفرّون من الذكر الذي فيه حياتهم ونجاتهم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"بَلْ يُرِيدُ كُلُّ امْرِيٕٖ مِّنْهُمْ أَن يُؤْتَىٰ صُحُفٗا مُّنَشَّرَةٗ","tradPropre":"Chacun d'eux voudrait plutôt qu'on lui apporte des feuilles tout étalées.","tradEn":"Rather, every person among them desires that he would be given scriptures spread about.","tradEs":"Ellos quisieran que descendieran [del cielo] páginas con un mensaje especial [que les confirmase que Mujámmad es un Mensajero de Dios].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Leur exigence orgueilleuse de recevoir chacun des manuscrits tout déployés venus du ciel,</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Why Verse 52 Was Revealed: Their Arrogant Demand for Personal Scrolls from Heaven.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Exegesis of Mujāhid & Qatādah:</strong> Certain leaders of Quraysh declared that they would not follow the Prophet ﷺ unless Jibrīl brought each of them a personal, unsealed scroll from Allāh addressed by name; Allāh exposed that their real motive was simply lack of fear of the Hereafter (v.53).","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Causa de revelación de la aleya 52: Su exigencia arrogante de pergaminos individuales.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comentario de Muyāhid y Qatādah:</strong> Algunos jefes de Quraysh dijeron que no creerían a menos que cada uno amaneciera con una carta abierta de Allah dirigida a su nombre; Allah reveló que su verdadero mal era no temer el Más Allá (v.53).","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>سبب نزول الآية 52 : طلب كبراء قريش صحفًا منشورة بأسمائهم.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>تفسير مجاهد وقتادة :</strong> قال نفر من مشركي قريش: لن نؤمن لك يا محمد حتى يصبح عند رأس كل رجل منا كتاب منشور من الله باسمه! فبيّن الله أن علة إعراضهم هي عدم خوفهم من الآخرة (آية 53).","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا بَل لَّا يَخَافُونَ الْأٓخِرَةَ","tradPropre":"Ah! Non! C'est plutôt qu'ils ne craignent pas l'au-delà.","tradEn":"No! But they do not fear the Hereafter.","tradEs":"Pero no se lo concederemos, porque no tienen temor devocional a la vida del más allá.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cela n’arrivera pas. La raison de leur égarement exagéré est qu’ils ne croient pas au châtiment de l’au-delà, demeurant de ce fait mécréants.","explicationEn":"53. The matter is not like that. In fact, the reason for their persistence in their misguidance is that they do not have faith in the punishment of the afterlife, so they remained in their disbelief.","explicationEs":"53. No les será concedido este libro que Allah bajó del cielo para ellos, porque la razón de su persistencia en su extravío es que no creen en el juicio de la otra vida, por lo que permanecen en su incredulidad.","explicationAr":"ليس الأمر كذلك، بل السبب في تماديهم في ضلالهم أنهم لا يؤمنون بعذاب الآخرة، فبقوا على كفرهم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"كَلَّآ إِنَّهُ تَذْكِرَةٞ","tradPropre":"Ah! Non! Ceci est vraiment un Rappel.","tradEn":"No! Indeed, the Qur'an is a reminder","tradEs":"[El Corán] es una exhortación","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce Coran est une rappel et conseil bienveillant et un rappel.","explicationEn":"54. Indeed, this Qur’ān is an admonition and a reminder.","explicationEs":"54. Este Corán es una advertencia y una exhortación.","explicationAr":"ألا إن هذا القرآن موعظة وتذكير.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"فَمَن شَآءَ ذَكَرَهُ","tradPropre":"Quiconque veut, qu'il se le rappelle.","tradEn":"Then whoever wills will remember it.","tradEs":"para que reflexione quien quiera.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque veut lire le Coran et en tirer des enseignements, qu’il le lise et en tire des enseignements.","explicationEn":"55. Whoever wishes to read the Qur’ān and take lesson from it does so.","explicationEs":"55. Quien quiera leer el Corán y aprender de él que lo haga.","explicationAr":"فمن شاء أن يقرأ القرآن ويتعظ به قرأه واتعظ به.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"وَمَا يَذْكُرُونَ إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ اللَّهُ هُوَ أَهْلُ التَّقْوَىٰ وَأَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ","tradPropre":"Mais ils ne se rappelleront que si Allah veut. C'est Lui qui est Le plus digne d'être craint; et c'est Lui qui détient le pardon.","tradEn":"And they will not remember except that Allah wills. He is worthy of fear and adequate for [granting] forgiveness.","tradEs":"Pero solo lo harán aquellos para quienes Dios quiera la guía. Solo Él es digno de ser adorado, y solo Él es la fuente del perdón.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Conclusion rappelant que nul ne se souvient que par la Volonté d'Allāh, Seul digne d'être craint et Détenteur du pardon.</strong>","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Allāh Is the Lord Worthy of Reverence and the Lord of Forgiveness (v.54–56).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadith of Anas ibn Mālik (At-Tirmidhī #3328 & Ibn Mājah #4249):</strong> Concludes the surah affirming that human remembrance is encompassed by Allāh's Will, and that He alone is worthy of being revered and obeyed (<em>Ahl at-Taqwā</em>) and worthy to forgive all who turn to Him in repentance (<em>Ahl al-Maghfirah</em>).","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Allah es Digno de ser temido y Digno de perdonar (v.54–56).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Anas ibn Mālik (At-Tirmidhī n°3328):</strong> Cierra la sura proclamando que sólo se recuerda por voluntad de Allah y que Él es Digno de reverencia (<em>Ahl at-Taqwā</em>) y Digno de perdonar a quien se vuelve a Él (<em>Ahl al-Maghfirah</em>).","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿هُوَ أَهْلُ التَّقْوَىٰ وَأَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ﴾ (آية 54-56).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong style='color:#ffffff;'>حديث أنس بن مالك (الترمذي 3328 وابن ماجه 4249) :</strong> خُتمت السورة بأن ذكر العبد إنما يكون بمشيئة الله وتوفيقه، وأنه سبحانه أهلٌ أن يُتّقى فلا يُعصى، وأهلٌ أن يغفر لمن تاب إليه وأناب.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-75-verset-1.html"}]};